:"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-05T01:10:05Z","updated_at":"2025-03-05T01:10:05Z","body":"> May be worth checking if the 2D editor have the same issue?\r\n\r\nThe 2D editor uses <kbd>Q</kbd>-<kbd>W</kbd>-<kbd>E</kbd>-<kbd>S</kbd> (<kbd>R</kbd> is used for the ruler, while we use <kbd>M</kbd> for that in 3D).\r\n\r\nWe should probably harmonize the 2D and 3D shortcuts (to make 2D act like 3D), but I'm not sure if it should be done here or in a separate PR.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2699450079/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2703485685","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103533#issuecomment-2703485685","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103533","id":2703485685,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hI-r1","user":{"login":"Nodragem","id":10520249,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTIwMjQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10520249?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem","html_url":"https://github.com/Nodragem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-06T10:48:19Z","updated_at":"2025-03-06T10:48:19Z","body":"I checked and in the 2D editor:\r\n- QWE are not physically binding while they should; \r\n- S is binded to (S)cale and R to (R)uler, and these ones should be kept as NOT physically binded.\r\n \r\nSo yes, there is a need for harmonization and that harmonization could be part of creating distinct QWER and GRS presets. By splitting into 2 presets, we can really harmonized the QWER approach, without worrying about GRS (and vice-versa).\r\n\r\nIn this PR (or another), we could still make sure that QWE in the 2D editor as physically binded. \r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2703485685/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2714591819","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103533#issuecomment-2714591819","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/1035